    <version>26.4.0</version>
    <time>1783015945</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to 26.4.0:
  - doc: update blockList stability status to release candidate
  - fs: support caller-supplied readFile() buffers
  - http: close pre-request sockets in closeIdleConnections
  - loader: implement package maps
  - net: support TCP_KEEPINTVL and TCP_KEEPCNT in setKeepAlive
  - tls: add certificateCompression option
  - vfs: dispatch node:fs/promises to mounted VFS instances
  - vfs: add minimal node:vfs subsystem
- Run obs-git-init (and add *-build directory to .gitignore)</comment>
    <requestid>1363512</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>1b6937a9dfbc2623cd25fb3bbbf519ae</srcmd5>
    <version>26.5.1</version>
    <time>1785705236</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>- Update to 26.5.1:
  - CVE-2026-56846: HTTP/2 retained headers can bypass maxSessionMemory limits (bsc#1272941)
  - CVE-2026-56848: HTTP/2 re-entrant send can cause heap-use-after-free (bsc#1272942)
  - CVE-2026-58043: Permission Model path matching can over-grant filesystem access (bsc#1272943)
  - CVE-2026-56850: HTTPS Agent can reuse mTLS identities across PFX certificates (bsc#1272944)
  - CVE-2026-58040: HTTPS Agent session reuse can skip hostname verification (bsc#1272945)
  - CVE-2026-58041: node:sqlite SQLTagStore iterator replay can re-execute writes (bsc#1272946)
  - CVE-2026-58042: dns.resolveAny() can abort on DNS responses with many A records (bsc#1272947)
  - CVE-2026-58045: node:zlib sync APIs can crash on spoofed TypedArray length (bsc#1272948)
  - CVE-2026-56847: Permission Model allows trace events to write outside the allowlist (bsc#1272949)
  - CVE-2026-58039: Permission Model allows process reports to write outside the allowlist (bsc#1272950)
  - CVE-2026-58044: HTTP parser header truncation can enable request smuggling (bsc#1272951)
- Changes in 26.5.0:
  - buffer: implement blob.textStream()
  - esm: add --experimental-import-text flag
  - perf_hooks: sample delay per event loop iteration
  - stream: expose ReadableStreamTee
  - tls: report negotiated TLS groups

- Add upstream patch to fix build on aarch64:
  * nodejs-add-missing-include.patch</comment>
    <requestid>1369027</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>d6f2d4a6983df58fe36019c26b142b5f</srcmd5>
    <version>26.7.0</version>
    <time>1787766932</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to 26.7.0:
  - crypto: support loading private keys through STORE loaders
  - lib: add perfetto support
  - module: implement Symbol.dispose in ModuleHooks
  - st_runner: add support for --test-coverage-include-all
For details, see https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases#release-v26.7.0
- fix_ci_tests.patch: look up libnode location instead of hardcoding it
- no_avx2_on_i586.patch: remove AVX2 from i586

- npm-line-truncation.patch: do not truncate long lines in help output (bsc#1276224)

- Add shared library (bsc#1174792)
- versioned.patch: use libnode.so.* instead of versioning it
  as soname is already unique between major versions
- no-rpath.patch: remove fixed RPATH

- Update to 26.6.0:
  - ffi: add getCurrentEventLoop
  - test_runner: add context.log() and test:log event
  - test_runner: report entryFile in TestStream events
- CVE-2026-54272: ip-address.patch: misclassification of IPv4-mapped/NAT64 IPv6 addresses allows for bypass of SSRF and trust-boundary checks (bsc#1272882)
- For details, see https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases#release-v26.6.0</comment>
    <requestid>1373780</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>c3d0474f20bf8451ef48547256a02e0b</srcmd5>
    <version>26.12.0</version>
    <time>1792609231</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to 26.12.0:
  - doc,lib,src: throw on missing WebAssembly or RX support
  - http: add websocketMask() and websocketUnmask()
for details see https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.12.0
nodejs-add-missing-include.patch: upstreamed, dropped

- Update to 26.11.1:
  - buffer: add isLatin1
  - buffer: add Buffer.stringLength()
  - http: add isValidHeaderName() and isValidHeaderValue()
  - http2: add connectionWindowSize option
  - perf_hooks: fix truncation of monitorEventLoopDelay() resolution
  - perf_hooks: allow RecordableHistogram to record 0
  - perf_hooks: add histogram.diff()
  - perf_hooks: add histogram.snapshot()
  - perf_hooks: harden histogram CBOR import validation
  - process: graduate process.ref/unref to stable
  - sqlite: rename DatabaseSync and StatementSync
  - src: add --process-timeout=N
  - src: expose size and count in heap profile output
  - src: let embedders exempt linked bindings from the addon permission
For complete list of changes, see
  https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.11.1
  https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.11.0
  https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.10.0
  https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.9.0
  https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.8.2
NOTICE: reject vuln reports on things that are enabled only by
`--experimental-*` runtime flag that are still works in progress.
https://github.com/nodejs/node/commit/ae1801eb55</comment>
    <requestid>1386755</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="6" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>a13f82015d794f2ee27a2e89e9d32b0f</srcmd5>
    <version>26.13.1</version>
    <time>1795519353</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to 26.13.1:
  - CVE-2026-123863 http2: release headers when a stream is removed (bsc#1290147)
  - CVE-2026-123864 tls,http: prevent nested parser execution from empty writes (bsc#1290148)
  - CVE-2026-123865 http2: detect streams abandoned by nghttp2 (bsc#1290149)
  - CVE-2026-123866 http2: retain buffers until socket writes finish (bsc#1290150)
  - CVE-2026-123872 tls: Client certificate authentication bypass via TLS renegotiation (bsc#1290154)
  - CVE-2026-123874 http2: retain streams during pending writes (bsc#1290155)
  - CVE-2026-126051 tls: fix remotely reachable TLS server crash (bsc#1290143)
  - CVE-2026-123828 http2: avoid overflowing ALTSVC buffers (bsc#1290144)
  - CVE-2026-123867 tls: apply the CA of SNI contexts without a certificate (bsc#1290151)
  - CVE-2026-123868 http2: charge inbound DATA retained by streams to maxSessionMemory (bsc#1290152)
  - CVE-2026-123871 http: redact proxy credentials in invalid proxy URL errors (bsc#1290153)
  - CVE-2026-123875 http2: guard against null write request on cancelled stream (bsc#1290156)
  - CVE-2026-123877 https: isolate Agent TLS policy keys (bsc#1290157)
  - CVE-2026-123829 permission: do not leak denied descendants in recursive fs.watch (bsc#1290145)
  - CVE-2026-123862 zlib: handle params callback after destroy (bsc#1290146)
  - CVE-2026-123873 permission: check heap snapshot destination (bsc#1290434)
  - deps: update to undici 8.12.4
    - CVE-2026-120474: cross-user cache disclosure via same-origin redirect (bsc#1290366)
    - CVE-2026-120222: Denial of Service via unhandled exception in cache-interceptor response replay (bsc#1290286)
    - CVE-2026-116630: cross-user information disclosure via cross-origin redirect revalidation (bsc#1290342)
    - CVE-2026-120415: cross-origin credential disclosure via array-of-tuples headers bypassing redirect stripping (bsc#1290319)
    - CVE-2026-120423: Subresource Integrity bypass via whitespace in integrity metadata (bsc#1290325)
    - CVE-2026-116592: cache poisoning and cross-user disclosure via intermediate redirect hops (bsc#1290357)
  - deps: update llhttp to 9.4.4
  - deps: update brotli to 1.2.1
  - deps: update sqlite to 3.54.1
- fix_ci_tests.patch: fix test-watch-mode.mjs on 32-bit
- ffi_32bit.patch: fix ffi tests on 32-bit
- icu_791.patch: fix compilation with icu 79.1 (bsc#1289933)

- Limit to z15+ arch (bsc#1289267)

- Update to 26.13.0:
  - first LTS version. No changes since 26.12.1

- Update to 26.12.1:
  - CVE-2026-106069, CVE-2026-106072 tls: reject non-canonical IP addresses (bsc#1286563, bsc#1286566)
  - CVE-2026-105482 dns: validate resolve inputs for null bytes (bsc#1286561)
  - CVE-2026-105483 tls: fix ip normalization regression (bsc#1286562)
  - CVE-2026-111497 deps: brotli: cherry-pick 0ed4268a4401abcb44720963 (bsc#1286564)
  - CVE-2026-105481 http: ensure agent data guard works without I/O (bsc#1286565)
  - CVE-2026-106074 crypto: reset random caches across snapshots (bsc#1286567)
  - CVE-2026-106070 zlib: avoid caching invalid ZIP local headers (bsc#1286568)
  - CVE-2026-106073 permission: check permission model in realpathSync (bsc#1286570)
  - CVE-2026-106071 permission: filesystem over-grant via wildcard radix lookup (bsc#1286569)
  - deps: V8: backport 93cd21e8254b
  - deps: update undici to 8.12.2
    (bsc#1285943, bsc#1285942, bsc#1285941, bsc#1285940, bsc#1285939, bsc#1285938, bsc#1285861,
     CVE-2026-109932, CVE-2026-109924, CVE-2026-109869, CVE-2026-109841, CVE-2026-109829, CVE-2026-109383, CVE-2026-87018,
	 bsc#1279834, CVE-2026-84961, CVE-2026-85024, CVE-2026-85008, CVE-2026-84947, CVE-2026-85152, CVE-2026-84890, CVE-2026-84933, CVE-2026-85014)
  - tls: reject chains containing blocked public keys
  - deps: update c-ares to 1.34.9 (where applicable)
  - tools: retry Gatekeeper check and stapling after notarization
  - crypto: harden X.509 conversion and formatting

- deps: update Undici to 8.10.2
  (bsc#1279523, bsc#1279522, bsc#1279513,
   CVE-2026-18149, CVE-2026-18540, CVE-2026-19534)
  - deps: update undici to 8.9.0
    (bsc#1273593, bsc#1273591,
	 CVE-2026-16728, CVE-2026-16729)</comment>
    <requestid>1398842</requestid>
